A||||5||MoneypitGT||Oil Cooler?||||5||
Z||000000||MoneypitGT||12-13-2001||11:13 PM||||So where does everyone put their oil cooler? I was thinking of running it up front but that would be a pain in the ass to change the oil, well atleast to get all of the oil out. Any thoughts on this?<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR>  <B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||5
Z||000001||ITB 2M4||12-14-2001||01:08 AM||||I took out the carpeting in the trunk, then cut a hole in the lower front half of the trunk, and mounted it there.  I put a mesh screen in front of it to keep the rocks from damaging it.  But this is for a race car, and you may not want to do that to a street car.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Blacktree||12-14-2001||02:11 AM||||Ideally, you want the oil cooler to be as close to the engine as possible. The longer the oil lines are, the more oil pressure you're going to lose. The two best places I can think of would be:<P>1) On the front side of the engine cradle (front in relation to the car, not the engine). It should get some decent airflow there. Just make sure you mount it so it's not hanging down from the cradle. That would be very unwise.<P>2) If you have side fender scoops or plan on getting them, you could mount the cooler inside the fender well inside the scoop. That should provide for some very good airflow (and hence very good cooling ability) but leaves it vulnerable to side impacts.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||12-14-2001||02:17 AM||||In between the block and filter.  I have the GM factory 3400 cooler.  Probably not as efficient as the air cooled, but uses lots less space.<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTDude||12-17-2001||09:26 AM||||The place that makes the most sense to me is on the right hand side of the engine compartment....exactly opposite of the air filter housing.  Add a scoop and your oil will be well cooled and it won't be a hassle to install.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||3
Z||000005||FieroJoe||12-17-2001||10:27 AM||||Any body got some pics of thier installs?  When I swap in a V6 soon, I want to do this and add a remote oil filter.  I am going to move the battery up front, so I was planning on putting in the oil filter where the battery used to be.||||reg||1
